<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38534" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prŏcus</span></b> , i (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen. plur.</i>
			procūm, <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 46, 156</span></i>), m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A wooer</i>, <i>suitor</i>: proci  dicuntur, qui poscunt aliquam in matrimonium, Graece
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνηστῆρες</span>. Est enim procare
			poscere, etc., <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 249</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">me natam nulli veterum sociare procorum Fas
					erat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Penelope difficilis procis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 10, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apotheca procis intacta est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. S.
					2, 5, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4, 794</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 10</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">14, 670</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proci loripedes, said of slow people,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Poen. 3, 1, 7</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of canvassers, <i>a
				suitor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impudentes proci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 96, 330</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
